;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">The decrease in interest expense from continuing operations in 2025 was primarily due to prepaying the remaining $75.0 million of the principal amount due under the 2027 Term Loans on May 8, 2024, partially offset by interest expense on the $38.7 million of </span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:27.35pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:23pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">68</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:91.06%;border:0;margin:30pt 4.47% 30pt 4.47%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:4.47%;padding-right:4.47%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:7.2pt;min-height:20.15pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;"><a style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';" href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">outstanding 2029 Term Loan principal and the LOQTORZI portion of the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement, both of which commenced on May 8, 2024 and incurred twelve months of interest during the year ended December 31, 2025.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">Interest expense from discontinued operations was $3.5 million and $16.4 million in 2025 and 2024, respectively, and was related to the 2026 Convertible Notes, the UDENYCA portion of the Revenue Purchase and Sale Agreement, and $175.0 million of the $250.0 million principal amount due under the 2027 Term Loans.</span></p><a id="_Hlk220523125"></a><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">We expect interest expense from continuing operations to be slightly lower in 2026 than in 2025, primarily as a result </span>of the downward trend in market interest rates relative to the 2025 period<span style="background:#ffffff;">.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-al